  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Clene’s lead candidate CNM-Au8 for ALS is advancing toward a potential accelerated approval, fueled by FDA feedback that neurofilament light (NfL) biomarker changes may support a New Drug Application. The planned NDA submission in mid‑2026 creates a binary catalyst in a high‑unmet‑need neurodegenerative disease market. While the drug has shown a favorable safety profile, the FDA has indicated more data is needed to solidify the biomarker‑outcome link, tempering the outlook with some regulatory uncertainty.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has proactively engaged the FDA and positioned the filing via the accelerated pathway, showing strategic discipline. An oversubscribed, multi‑tranche financing extended the cash runway through a potential NDA acceptance decision, mitigating near‑term funding risk and demonstrating the market’s willingness to support the story. Despite mixed analyst commentary—ranging from strong buy ratings to a cautionary sell—management’s execution of the regulatory roadmap and capital preservation efforts have bolstered credibility headed into the pivotal application window.",
